- op: discuss  # db28
  at: '2026-08-28T00:21:15Z'  # db28
  by: agent  # db28
  actor: jgstern_agent  # db28
  clock: 3  # db28
  nonce: db28  # db28
  message: "SATISFIED on the merged tree (dev 1a3145c9f0), PR #587.\n\nBEHAVIOURAL EVIDENCE, control in the same run. Four purpose-built repositories\nthrough the shipped verify-claims CLI:\n  repro   os.environ.get() only ....... 2 rows -> 1, keeps os.environ.get\n  repro   BOTH forms in one symbol .... 2 rows -> 1\n  repro   sys.stdout.write(x) ......... 2 rows -> 1, keeps sys.stdout.write\n  CONTROL bare os.environ[\"X\"] ........ 1 row  -> 1, still os.environ\nAll four return verdict=violated, so the runs are not vacuously inert.\n\nTHE PREMISE WAS RIGHT AND THE CAUSE IS NOT THE MATCHER. Read the IR first: the\nanalyzer emits TWO EDGES for the one expression --\n  module_attribute_reference -> python:os:0-0:os.environ:external_symbol\n  ast_call_direct            -> python:os.environ:0-0:get:external_symbol\nso each matches its own row. Fixed by subsuming a parent whose qualified name\nis the MODULE SLOT of another entry matched at the SAME caller. The relation is\ncomputed from the catalogue, so a user-supplied catalogue with the shape is\ncovered without a table to maintain.\n\nTWO THINGS THIS ITEM DID NOT HAVE, both from checking analogues.\n  1. IT IS SYMMETRIC. The item measured only the source side. Of the four rows\n     with the shape, TWO ARE SINKS -- sys.stdout and sys.stderr under logging\n     (sys.stdin is a source under ipc_recv) -- so sys.stdout.write(x) doubles a\n     sink exactly as os.environ.get() doubles a source.\n  2. IT IS NOT ROW-UNIT-ONLY, and the item's \"situation count is unaffected\" is\n     wrong in general. collapse_unadjudicated_flows runs on\n     {structural, ddg_mixed}; a confirmed ddg walk IS a pair claim and passes\n     through untouched, so on the ddg arm the two rows never merged and the\n     read was reported as two SITUATIONS. 0005's population was structural and\n     ddg_mixed, which is why it read as row-only THERE. Both arms are pinned.\n\nSCOPE-NOT-MEASURED IS NOW MEASURED, which was the item's own open question.\nEnumerated all 15 shipped catalogues for the parent/slot-family shape. It\nexists in exactly FOUR rows, ALL PYTHON: os.environ (env_read), sys.stdin\n(ipc_recv), sys.stdout and sys.stderr (logging). bash, go, javascript and rust\nare pinned at zero by a parametrised test, so a catalogue that later grows the\nshape fires rather than silently doubling.\n\nA/B ON THE TWO REPOSITORIES THIS ITEM NAMES, per-arm cache, arms strictly\nsequential, each arm PROVEN before it ran:\n  mitmproxy  summed collapsed_flow_count 29 -> 20 (-31.0%), 6 of 12 rows moved\n  poetry     summed collapsed_flow_count  5 ->  3 (-40.0%), 1 of  2 rows moved\nEvery moved row shows the filed shape exactly:\n  ['os.environ', 'os.environ.get'] -> ['os.environ.get']\nCONTROL: 8 of 8 claim verdicts unchanged, with violated on both repositories,\nand evidence_count / flow_origins / excluded_flows / sanitized_flows all\nunchanged. Situation counts did not move on either repository.\n\nA NEAR-MISS RECORDED: my first verdict comparison read a field named `status`\nthat came back None on BOTH arms -- a null reading as \"no change\". The real\nfield is `verdict`. The numbers above are from the real field.\n\nDISCLOSED LIMITATION: what is deducted is a NAME, not a flow. Where both forms\ngenuinely occur in one symbol -- 2 of the 7 situations this item measured -- the\ntwo edges are indistinguishable from the single-form case, because edges are\ndeduplicated on (src, dst, edge_type) per INV-vukiv and the multiplicity is gone\nbefore taint sees it. The coarser name is dropped, the finding is still\nreported, and no verdict moves.\n\nTagged awaits_bakeoff_validation: the -31% / -40% is measured on two named\nrepositories, not on a broad corpus, so whether it generalises is unvalidated."  # db28
