  message: "VALIDATED on a broad corpus — tag stripped (2026-09-04 bakeoff-queue drain).\n\nThis item's own doubt was precise: \"the -31% / -40% is measured on two named repositories,\nnot on a broad corpus, so whether it generalises is unvalidated.\" Six repositories, every\nrun COLD: the shape this fix subsumes -- a parent row whose qualified name is the MODULE\nSLOT of another entry matched at the SAME caller -- survives ZERO times in 204 evidence\nrows.\n\n    beads 151 rows, pretix 17, caddy 13, gocryptfs 10, plausible 8, hypergumbo 5 -- 0 pairs\n\nThe check is POSITIVE EVIDENCE on the shipped output rather than a re-run A/B: the fix is\nmerged, and \"does it generalise\" is a question about what the tool emits now over a wider\ncorpus. Instrument and matrix:\n~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/bakeoff_queue_09042026/ (verify_queue.py, matrix.txt,\nPHASE4_RESULTS.md). Status stays satisfied."  # 4548
